{"sections":[],"kind":"article","seeAlsoSections":[{"title":"How-to Guides","anchor":"How-to-Guides","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/HowToAddAPaywall","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/HowToAddAVersionKillswitch","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/HowToAddAParentalGate","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/HowToAddAnalytics","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/HowToAddPersistence","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/HowToAddICloudSync","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/BuildingADomainPlugin","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/AgentSkill"],"generated":true}],"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"patch":0,"major":0},"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/HowToAddFeatureFlags"},"metadata":{"title":"Add Feature Flags","roleHeading":"Article","role":"article","modules":[{"name":"Swidux"}]},"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/swidux\/howtoaddfeatureflags"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"primaryContentSections":[{"content":[{"text":"Overview","type":"heading","level":2,"anchor":"Overview"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"SwiduxFeatureFlags","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" is a domain plugin that owns a "},{"code":"FeatureFlagsState","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" slice, fetches a Swidux-defined JSON wire format via a provider-agnostic ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"FeatureFlagsService"},{"type":"text","text":", and answers reads against state. Bucketing is pure FNV-1a — same input always produces the same bucket, no network round-trip per read. Local overrides give QA a one-action toggle that wins over remote evaluation."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"For an API-level reference, see ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PluginFeatureFlagsReference","isActive":true},{"text":". For where domain plugins fit in the dispatch cycle, see ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PluginArchitecture"},{"text":".","type":"text"}]},{"text":"Before you start","type":"heading","level":2,"anchor":"Before-you-start"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"This guide assumes you have a Swidux app already wired up — "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"AppState"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"AppAction"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"AppReducer"},{"text":", and ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"AppStore"},{"text":" exist and the store is in the SwiftUI environment. If you’re not there yet, follow ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/GettingStarted"},{"type":"text","text":" first."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"You also need somewhere to host a JSON file. Any URL works — Cloudflare Pages, R2, S3, a Worker, your own backend. The plugin doesn’t care. "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Examples\/ConfigWorker\/"},{"text":" is a runnable Cloudflare Worker that serves feature-flag ","type":"text"},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"text":"and","type":"text"}]},{"text":" killswitch config for every app in a portfolio from one URL and one KV namespace, keyed ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"GET \/<appID>\/<resource>"},{"type":"text","text":" — point this plugin at "},{"code":"https:\/\/<host>\/<appID>\/flags","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"."}]},{"anchor":"Step-1-Add-the-dependency","type":"heading","text":"Step 1: Add the dependency","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Add the ","type":"text"},{"code":"SwiduxFeatureFlags","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" product to your app target in ","type":"text"},{"code":"Package.swift","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":":","type":"text"}]},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":[".target(","    name: \"MyApp\",","    dependencies: [","        \"Swidux\",","        \"SwiduxFeatureFlags\",","    ]",")"]},{"level":2,"anchor":"Step-2-Add-a-state-slice-and-action-case","type":"heading","text":"Step 2: Add a state slice and action case"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"In ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"AppState.swift"},{"type":"text","text":":"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["import SwiduxFeatureFlags","","@Swidux","nonisolated struct AppState: Equatable, Sendable {","    @Slice var featureFlags: FeatureFlagsState = .init()","    \/\/ ... your other slices","}"]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"In ","type":"text"},{"code":"AppAction.swift","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":":"}]},{"type":"codeListing","code":["enum AppAction: Sendable {","    case featureFlags(FeatureFlagsAction)","    \/\/ ... your other cases","}"],"syntax":"swift"},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"import SwiduxFeatureFlags"},{"text":" is needed in ","type":"text"},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"every"}]},{"text":" file that touches ","type":"text"},{"code":"store.featureFlags.*","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" or ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"FeatureFlagsAction"},{"text":" — including views that read flags for display. ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@_exported import Swidux"},{"text":" re-exports core Swidux only, not plugin modules. See ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PluginArchitecture","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":".","type":"text"}]}],"type":"aside","style":"tip","name":"Tip"},{"type":"heading","level":2,"anchor":"Step-3-Hydrate-state-and-register-the-plugin","text":"Step 3: Hydrate state and register the plugin"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"At app launch, mint a stable per-install "},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"device ID"}],"type":"strong"},{"type":"text","text":" (Keychain-backed so it survives reinstall — this is the bucketing identity), hydrate state from your "},{"code":"KeyValueStore","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" (so the last-known-good config survives cold launches), then register the plugin. Add ","type":"text"},{"code":"var deviceID: String = \"\"","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" to ","type":"text"},{"code":"AppState","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and point ","type":"text"},{"code":"deviceIDKeyPath","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" at it:"}]},{"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing","code":["let kv = UserDefaultsKeyValueStore()                       \/\/ flags config cache","","\/\/ Stable bucketing identity — Keychain so it survives reinstall, and shared","\/\/ with analytics: AnalyticsIdentity(userID: \\.deviceID, …).","let deviceID = KeychainKeyValueStore(service: \"com.example.app\").deviceIdentity()","","let initial = AppState(","    featureFlags: .hydrated(from: kv, deviceID: deviceID),","    deviceID: deviceID",")","","let store = Store(initialState: initial, reducer: AppReducer())","","\/\/ With the Examples\/ConfigWorker setup this is the shared portfolio URL:","\/\/ \"https:\/\/<host>\/<appID>\/flags\". Any URL returning FeatureFlagsConfig works.","let configURL = URL(static: \"https:\/\/<host>\/<appID>\/flags\")","","let flags = FeatureFlagsPlugin<AppState, AppAction>(","    state: \\.featureFlags,","    action: AppAction.featureFlags,","    extractAction: { if case .featureFlags(let a) = $0 { return a } else { return nil } },","    service: HTTPFeatureFlagsService(url: configURL),","    deviceIDKeyPath: \\.deviceID,","    keyValueStore: kv",")","store.register(plugin: flags)"]},{"type":"heading","level":2,"anchor":"Step-4-Declare-typed-flag-keys","text":"Step 4: Declare typed flag keys"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Declare each flag once on a namespace so reads are type-safe:"}]},{"syntax":"swift","code":["extension BoolFlag {","    static let newOnboarding = BoolFlag(\"new_onboarding\")","}","","enum CheckoutVariant: String { case control, treatment }","","extension VariantFlag where Variant == CheckoutVariant {","    static let checkoutLayout = VariantFlag(\"checkout_layout\", default: .control)","}","","extension ValueFlag where Value == Int {","    static let maxFreeUploads = ValueFlag(\"max_free_uploads\", default: 5)","}"],"type":"codeListing"},{"level":2,"type":"heading","text":"Step 5: Read flags from views","anchor":"Step-5-Read-flags-from-views"},{"type":"codeListing","code":["if store.featureFlags.isEnabled(.newOnboarding) {","    NewOnboardingView()","}","","let layout = store.featureFlags.variant(of: .checkoutLayout)","let cap = store.featureFlags.value(of: .maxFreeUploads)"],"syntax":"swift"},{"level":2,"type":"heading","text":"Step 6: Refresh on foreground","anchor":"Step-6-Refresh-on-foreground"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The plugin debounces "},{"code":".refresh","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" against the configured "},{"code":"RefreshPolicy","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", so it’s safe to dispatch on every "},{"code":"scenePhase","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" transition:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":[".onChange(of: scenePhase) { _, phase in","    if phase == .active { store.send(.featureFlags(.refresh)) }","}"]},{"level":2,"type":"heading","text":"Step 7: Guard against forever flags","anchor":"Step-7-Guard-against-forever-flags"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Give every flag a required owner and expiry, and add one CI test that fails when a flag outlives its expiry. Declare a manifest alongside the typed keys — the factory ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"owner"},{"type":"text","text":"\/"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"expires"},{"type":"text","text":" parameters are non-optional, and the keys are single-sourced from the flag declarations:"}]},{"code":["enum FlagManifest {","    static let all: [FlagDescriptor] = [","        .bool(.newOnboarding, owner: \"growth\",","              expires: Date(timeIntervalSince1970: 1_788_000_000), purpose: \"New onboarding flow\"),","        .variant(.checkoutLayout, owner: \"checkout\",","                 expires: Date(timeIntervalSince1970: 1_785_000_000), purpose: \"Checkout A\/B\"),","        .value(.maxFreeUploads, owner: \"platform\",","               expires: Date(timeIntervalSince1970: 1_785_000_000), purpose: \"Free upload cap\"),","    ]","}","","@Test func noForeverFlags() {","    let report = FlagGovernance.expirationReport(FlagManifest.all)","    #expect(report == nil, \"\\(report ?? \"\")\")   \/\/ failure names each expired flag + owner","}"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"This is a pure compile-time \/ test concern — no wire-format change and no effect on runtime evaluation."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"For wire format, bucketing, exposure tracking, and governance details, see "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PluginFeatureFlagsReference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"type":"paragraph"}],"kind":"content"}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux"]]},"abstract":[{"text":"Wire the ","type":"text"},{"code":"SwiduxFeatureFlags","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" plugin into a Swidux app for typed feature flags, A\/B variants, and remote-tunable scalar values from a single JSON config.","type":"text"}],"references":{"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/AgentSkill":{"type":"topic","kind":"article","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/agentskill","role":"article","title":"Using the Swidux Agent Skill","abstract":[{"text":"Install the bundled ","type":"text"},{"code":"swidux-ref","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" skill so your AI coding assistant has Swidux’s architecture rules and code templates on hand.","type":"text"}],"i